Atlantic Canada QSO Party -- the 47 counties and divisions (NL 11, PE 3, NB 15, NS 18), issue 116.
The sponsor rules (V 26.0.1) give the counts and send the codes to the acqp.ca resources page, which refuses automated fetches.
Codes from DXLog.net ACQP.txt (updated 2026-09-06), names from the ham2k qso-parties data (not sponsor verified); see
docs/ContestRules/QSOParties/AtlanticCanada/AC-QSO-PARTY-Counties.txt. Each line maps its county or division to its province
with a greater-than sign. Out of the region each is its own multiplier (FCONTEST sets MultipliersIsCounties). In the region
a county counts as its province, and the ADIF STATE of a county is that province.
No INCLUDE here: an out-of-region entrant table must hold only counties and divisions. No line of this header may hold an equals sign.

